    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 48a56b23a7d7bd0cf9b08f87655db9d817a71fc1 -->\n**Review of head `48a56b23a`: clean.** The coordinator read the diff: one rule and its comment in `.gitattributes`, in the form of the `.nc` rule above it. No other file changes, and no blob is renormalised.\n\nEvidence from the author's run (git commands only): before the rule, a checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` gives `i/lf w/crlf` for `examples/catalog/2d/drill-overfeed/refusal.txt`; with the rule it gives `i/lf w/lf attr/text eol=lf`. This is the only `refusal.txt` in the catalog.\n\nNo build ran: the change is one attribute line and has no effect on an LF checkout. The post-merge run is the check of the tip. The reporter confirms on his checkout (#3628).\n",
